# Source manifest — reproducible-by-reference (Invariant 3).
# Re-clone at build time; the working tree under sources/codex/ is gitignored.
#
# TOOLCHAIN SOURCE — a tool this repo actually RUNS (#81, ingested 2026-08-02).
#
# ⚠️ INVARIANT: this pin MUST track the version we actually run.
#   version source: mise.toml `[tools] codex`
#   pinned here:    0.148.0
# Note the tag prefix: releases are `rust-v<version>`, so `ref` is NOT the bare
# version the two lines above name. Also: this manifest read 0.146.0 while
# mise.toml ran 0.146.1, i.e. it was ALREADY drifting before the 0.147.0 bump —
# back then the invariant above was stated in 13 manifests and enforced by
# nothing. The manifest check in `kb-currency-check` now enforces it, with the
# `rust-v` prefix handled via the spec's `tag_prefix` (#245).
# A pin that drifts from the installed version makes the corpus answer questions
# about code we are not running. Not hypothetical — `sources/graphify.manifest`
# records exactly that failure: it sat two releases behind for weeks, so every
# "how does graphify work?" answer came from the wrong source.
#
# Pin the RELEASE TAG, never a branch head — a branch drifts ahead of the release.
# To bump: change the version in its source above, then
#   git ls-remote --tags --refs https://github.com/openai/codex | grep <version>
# and set ref/commit here to match, then `mise run kb-build`.
#
# kind = code: AST extraction only, no LLM, no cost. NOTE this extracts the
# SOURCE and skips every .md by design — the tool's DOCS are a separate
# `kind = docs` mirror (#123), not this manifest.
url = https://github.com/openai/codex
ref = rust-v0.148.0
commit = ab52d1794d47d47ecaeb0ec37fc00fa31593ecf3
kind = code
added = 2026-08-02
# EXCLUDED FROM THE BUILD 2026-08-20 (Ray's ruling: skip any blocker, file it,
# and triage after the graphify extraction). Not a de-registration: the pin above
# stays committed and fingerprinted, and the INVARIANT above still binds — this
# manifest must keep tracking the version we run, skipped or not.
#
# ⚠️ THIS IS A TOOLCHAIN SOURCE, so the loss has a specific shape: while skipped,
# the corpus cannot answer questions about a tool this repo actually RUNS. That
# is the failure the invariant above was written to prevent, arrived at from the
# other direction. Tracked in #417.
#
# `kb-build` fails closed on ONE file: `Cargo.toml` produced zero nodes (#1666).
# One entry would normally be trivial, but the reviewed-metadata approver is
# JSON-only by construction — `graphify_sdk` calls `extract_json(path)` on every
# inventory item and compares graphify's own `skipped` disposition — so a TOML
# file cannot be approved through it without new machinery.
# Restore by deleting these two lines.
build = skip
skip_reason = #417: Cargo.toml produces zero nodes (#1666) and the reviewed-metadata approver is JSON-only, so a TOML file needs new machinery; skipped under Ray's 2026-08-20 ruling. TOOLCHAIN source, so the corpus cannot describe a tool we run while this holds
